team, for Pete's sake,

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:45.048
I would have picked you, Kelly.

00:01:45.048 --> 00:01:46.381
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:46.381 --> 00:01:48.240
- I love that you can
just do voices like that.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.250
So wait, how did you get
into doing cartoon voices?

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.190
- Okay, I'd say cartoon
voices got into me, really,

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.962
because I didn't really grow up thinking

00:01:54.962 --> 00:01:56.630
like "I'm gonna be a cartoon.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.475
I'm gonna go be a cartoon one day."

00:01:58.475 --> 00:02:00.270
- I know, it's a random job to get into.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.910
- Yeah. I mean, I'd done movies.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:04.301
I did a lot of different movies
and my thing was characters.

00:02:04.301 --> 00:02:06.940
And so I could, as you know, as a singer,

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.170
you can contort your voice.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.820
And I don't know what happened.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:10.840
I just, I did a play.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.250
I got to do all these
different voices in a play.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.780
And then suddenly someone
heard me in the play

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.880
